From 91d3ab059733710d35a45eb017421a6bde3964d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 19:40:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] AI cost tracking: real token counts + dollar cost,
 disclosed to the ledger

Item 4 of Wm's July 28 roadmap, first of its three remaining pieces (AI cost
tracking / recommendation-impact testing / lease-heartbeat). Wm's decisions,
2026-07-31: track token counts AND computed dollar cost (not tokens alone),
and disclose to the ledger as a real audit-trail fact (not just returned
in-memory).

New module ai_cost_tracking.py: MODEL_PRICING is a snapshot fetched fresh
from platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/pricing this session (not
recalled from training data -- pricing drifts and this is financial code).
cost_of_call() never guesses an unpriced model's rate from a similarly-named
one -- an unlisted model returns cost_usd=None with unpriced_reason naming
it, same 'say why it's unknown, never guess' discipline as event_v1.py's
Provenance Rule.

claude_governance_api.py is the only place in the repo that calls the real
Claude API (4 methods on ClaudeGovernanceDecider). All four now capture
'usage' off the response and attach a 'cost' dict to every returned
decision, including parse-failure paths (the call still cost money even
when the JSON that came back didn't parse). Found and fixed a real bug
along the way: usage/model_identity need to be bound BEFORE the try block,
or a genuine transport error (raised by messages.create itself) hits
NameError in the except clause instead of degrading to cost=None -- would
have been a new crash-on-network-hiccup path in code that's supposed to be
fail-closed.

Ledger side: ai_cost joins the shared canonical_fields.py contract as Item
8, same optional-hashed-field pattern every prior field (cassette_hash,
model_identity, authorized_by, ...) already uses -- legacy rows hash
byte-identically, no backfill, no chain break. Found a THIRD site that
needed updating beyond the two the module's own docstring names (writer +
twin-witness): PostgreSQLLedger.verify_chain() builds its own explicit
column list for self-verification and would have made every cost-bearing
row look tampered without this fix. Also surfaced ai_cost in get_decisions(),
the read-only audit API.

production_harness.py: the one live call site (safety_check, inside
process_call) now threads claude_decision.get('cost') through to the
ledger record as Item 8.

27 new tests across 4 files (pricing arithmetic, wiring into all 4 decider
methods including the transport-error regression, ledger hash/verify/read,
and one true end-to-end test through the live harness). Full suite 731
passed / 6 skipped, twice back-to-back. Ruff clean; bandit's only finding
anywhere in the touched files is the pre-existing dev-default password at
ledger_postgres.py:115 (untouched by this change).
